Subject: coercing inla.mesh to Spatial* object
Message-ID: <z1n1exlZrKM.e5fiiVOeDwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/z1n1exlZrKM/m/e5fiiVOeDwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Is it possible to coerce an inla.mesh to a Spatial* object (e.g., SpatialPolygonsDataFrame)? I like to retain the polygons to use in other packages (e.g., tmap, ggplot2, etc).

Thanks!

From uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com  Fri Jan  4 15:57:58 2019
From: uafb003e064114795 at groups.google.com (Finn Lindgren)
Date: Fri, 04 Jan 2019 15:57:58 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] coercing inla.mesh to Spatial* object
Message-ID: <z1n1exlZrKM.YGBlCjJHEAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <z1n1exlZrKM.e5fiiVOeDwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <z1n1exlZrKM.e5fiiVOeDwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/z1n1exlZrKM/m/YGBlCjJHEAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is no SpatialTriangulation class unfortunately, so it would need to be a SpatialPolygons object. I never wrote such a converter, but we have implemented ggplot2 geoms for inla.mesh objects in the inlabru package; see the tutorials/workshop materials on inlabru.org <http://inlabru.org> for examples. For basic plotting of just the mesh,
ggplot() + gg(mesh)
should do it, but it can also map functions defined on the mesh vertices, etc.

I can see the benefit of having an explicit object conversion though. I’ll put it on my list...

Finn

