I’d like to fit a point process model where I have observations of a point process realization as well as some areal counts on partial areas  of the domain . That is, I have

where

is the intensity field of the inhomogeneous Poisson process. I then have an observed point process. Following Chapter 4 of the SPDE book <https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-lcox.html>, I can fit this with INLA.

I would like to extend this to include additional observations of total counts within quadrats, of the form

This isn’t linear in the predictor, as discussed in the Spatial misalignment <https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/r-inla-discussion-group/change$20of$20support%7Csort:date/r-inla-discussion-group/TdATCDb6QUA/igfMrdhm9UYJ> discussion, so can’t be fit using INLA. But if I remember the ISEC workshop this past summer correctly, inlabru can deal with nonlinearities like this. Is it possible to define a likelihood that includes the change of support and the nonlinear transformation of the spatial field in inlabru to fit this model?

