From u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com  Sat Jan 12 16:54:16 2019
From: u3eab71733027a24a at groups.google.com (Helpdesk)
Date: Sat, 12 Jan 2019 16:54:16 +0000
Subject: Re: [r-inla] Computing exceedance probability
Message-ID: <a9d8wNEhWN4.gNNOa6nkCAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <a9d8wNEhWN4.d0187huWBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <a9d8wNEhWN4.198XdWSaQvEJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com> <a9d8wNEhWN4.d0187huWBQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/a9d8wNEhWN4/m/gNNOa6nkCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Either use

	inla.posterior.sample()

or use linear-combinations to extract such information.

with linear combinations, you get the marginal, and you can use
inla.pmarginal()  to compute the CDF.

for linear combinations, see the FAQ at r-inla.org <http://r-inla.org>

H

