Subject: Re: [r-inla] bym2 inla.posterior.sample control quantization?
Message-ID: <vYmjeuP0KeI.zoWdZOtHCQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <vYmjeuP0KeI._tin8v35BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <vYmjeuP0KeI._tin8v35BQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/vYmjeuP0KeI/m/zoWdZOtHCQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

with inla.posterior.sample(), only the integration points for the
hyperparameters in the INLA approximation
 are used as sample candidates.  If you need more complete samples for
the hyperparameters (but not simultaneously the latent variables), you
can use inla.hyperpar.sample() instead.

Finn

